@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Copyright Policy & Intellectual Property Protection";
}

<section class="legal-page">
    <div class="container container-narrow">
        <div class="legal-header">
            <div class="hero-tag">
                <span class="badge-tag badge-tag">© Intellectual Property</span>
            </div>
            <h1 class="legal-title">Copyright Policy</h1>
            <div class="legal-meta">
                <span>Compliance: Berne Convention &bull; WIPO Copyright Treaty &bull; DMCA</span>
                <span>Last Updated: August 31, 2026</span>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="legal-content">
            <div class="highlight-box">
                <strong>Our Commitment:</strong> Stream Helper deeply respects the intellectual property rights of content creators, film producers, independent artists, and digital broadcasters worldwide.
            </div>

            <h2>1. Neutral Technology Architecture</h2>
            <p>Stream Helper is a client-side media transport protocol analyzer, similar in function to web browsers, developer network inspectors, and standard download managers. The software does not host, store, index, promote, or distribute any video or audio files.</p>

            <h2>2. User Responsibility &amp; Authorization</h2>
            <p>All download operations are initiated solely and unilaterally by individual end users. Users are exclusively responsible for verifying that they possess the necessary rights, licenses, or statutory permissions to record or archive any media accessed through the software.</p>

            <h2>3. Protection Against Copyright Infringement</h2>
            <p>We actively discourage copyright infringement and emphasize that Stream Helper must not be used to create unauthorized copies of commercial content. Specifically:</p>
            <ul>
                <li>The software does not provide search engines or directories of copyrighted videos.</li>
                <li>The software does not bypass commercial Digital Rights Management (DRM) encryption systems.</li>
                <li>The software is distributed for legitimate educational, fair-use, and authorized private archiving purposes.</li>
            </ul>

            <h2>4. Third-Party Trademarks</h2>
            <p>All product names, trademarks, and registered trademarks mentioned on this website and in software documentation (including YouTube, Vimeo, Twitch, and others) are the property of their respective owners. Their mention does not imply any affiliation, sponsorship, or endorsement by those entity holders.</p>

            <h2>5. Notice for Rights Holders</h2>
            <p>If you are a copyright owner or an authorized agent representing one, and you have questions regarding the technical operation of Stream Helper, please review our <a asp-controller="Legal" asp-action="DMCA">DMCA &amp; Takedown Policy</a> or contact us directly at <a href="mailto:copyright@streamhelper.app">copyright@streamhelper.app</a>.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
